To ensure the reliability and traceability of our solution's outputs, we will leverage our existing secure software development life cycle (SDLC) practices, including code review, dependency scanning, secrets management, and periodic penetration testing conducted by an external provider of equivalent CREST level. Our vulnerability management process includes remediation SLAs by severity, and we have an incident response plan in place that covers detection, notification, and remediation, including adherence to the 72-hour GDPR breach-notification workflow.

Given our ISO 27001 certification since 2023, which covers development, delivery, and operations, and our ISO 27701 certification for privacy information management extension, we are well-equipped to handle the confidentiality and security requirements of client data. Our Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointment and maintenance of a data processing register, along with having a Data Processing Agreement (DPA) available that aligns with GDPR Article 28, further reinforce our commitment to GDPR compliance.

Overall, our existing measures provide a robust foundation for meeting the tender's security, confidentiality, and explainability requirements.
