Innovation strategies to propose for enhancing the quality of service could involve iterative methodologies that start with corpus curation with the firm's experts, followed by retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and an evaluation loop. This approach allows for continuous improvement based on feedback and performance metrics such as groundedness, relevance, factual support, and correctness of cited figures.

Moreover, considering our model options, which include a sovereign European open-weight model for full auditability and reliability, or top-tier proprietary models via API for higher performance, we can select the best model per engagement to balance performance with explainability and sovereignty needs. This flexibility supports tailored innovation strategies that cater to specific requirements while maintaining high standards of service quality.

Lastly, our approach to personalisation and data use, primarily through corpus curation and retrieval/prompt configuration without requiring training on personal or client data, ensures that innovations are adapted to the firm's specific context while respecting data privacy and compliance terms defined with the firm and its compliance function.
