Our platform's ability to perform multi-document synthesis and structured extraction with source linking enhances handling of client files by synthesizing information from multiple sources and extracting key figures or data points while linking them back to their original source passages. This not only aids in the preparation of comprehensive and accurate documents but also supports collaboration among professionals by providing a clear, traceable, and reliable basis for discussion and decision-making.

The requirement for response time below 2 seconds for common queries is fully covered as our platform has a p95 latency of 2.5 seconds or less, which can be achieved with appropriate model option and hosting tier selection. High availability during business hours with resilience to seasonal peak loads is also fully covered, given that our platform offers high availability on the appropriate hosting tier, with active-active redundancy across two availability zones and the ability to scale horizontally to handle peak loads.

Integration with accounting-production software, payroll software, document management / GED, and electronic-invoicing / dematerialisation environment via API-type interfaces is fully covered through our business tool integration capabilities, which include connectors and adapters for these systems, facilitated by our delivery partner Ligeo Conseil. User directory (SSO) integration is also fully covered as we support SAML and OIDC for single sign-on and can integrate with LDAP and Entra ID user directories.

To meet the tender requirements, we already have in place several necessary security measures. For data protection, we utilize encryption in transit with TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest with AES-256, with key management handled through our EU-based infrastructure. We also implement strict partitioning with logical isolation per client and per mission, preventing any cross-client circulation of data. Additionally, pseudonymisation is used where relevant, and we adhere to data minimization principles. Our hosting partner, OuraneCloud, provides a SecNumCloud compliant layer, ensuring sovereign hosting of confidential data within the EU.

For auditability and explainability, our product Atelier supports internal quality control and statutory audit review. It also maintains an audit log, allows for retrieval trace, and figure source linking, ensuring that all outputs are grounded in sources and can be traced back. Furthermore, we have no ungrounded numeric output. Our existing secure software development life cycle (SDLC) practices, including code review, dependency scanning, secrets management, and periodic penetration testing conducted by an external provider of equivalent CREST level, ensure the reliability and traceability of our solution's outputs.

Given our ISO 27001 certification since 2023, which covers development, delivery, and operations, and our ISO 27701 certification for privacy information management extension, we are well-equipped to handle the confidentiality and security requirements of client data. Our Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointment and maintenance of a data processing register, along with having a Data Processing Agreement (DPA) available that aligns with GDPR Article 28, further reinforce our commitment to GDPR compliance.

Our company is compliant with the regulatory requirements outlined as we ensure our contractual framework does not place us in a position that could compromise our professional obligations. However, we should flag potential risks related to data protection and confidentiality breaches, ensuring our GDPR compliance measures including Article 28 processing agreements are in place. Additionally, we must ensure strict adherence to auditor independence and separation of duties rules to avoid any conflicts of interest.

Our budget envelope for this project is €220,000 over 3 years, with 40% allocated to one-off project costs in the first year and 60% to recurring run costs over 3 years. To maintain a healthy margin, our target gross margin range is between 25% and 35%. By favouring cost-efficient tiers and models that protect the gross margin and the predictability of recurring costs, such as the sovereign tier with the sovereign European model, we can propose a cost-optimised approach.

To align with environmental considerations, we can leverage our existing sustainability practices, such as our green hosting partnership with OuraneCloud in the EU, which utilizes renewable energy and has a power usage effectiveness of 1.2, along with heat reuse capabilities. Additionally, we practice digital sobriety through model right-sizing, caching, and batching, which contribute to reducing our environmental footprint. Our carbon reporting capability also allows us to monitor and report on the deployment footprint, ensuring transparency.

Our proposal is structured around a pilot phase on one office or one mission line, followed by progressive generalisation, with change-management support and training provided. We aim to have a pilot operational before the next closing / tax campaign. By combining our technical capabilities, security measures, regulatory compliance, cost-optimised approach, and commitment to sustainability, we believe that Faber IA's Atelier platform is well-positioned to meet Cabinet Vauclair & Associés' needs for an artificial-intelligence assistance solution that improves productivity and quality of work while preserving professional secrecy and reliability.
